# Opinion

Meeting: 0008-start-web-client
Agent: ArchitectA
Task: start web client
Context:
- We are kicking off the HTML + JS client as the first frontend against the CalendarApp spec.
- The backend remains in Python; for now we will showcase flows with an in-memory JS mirror and DSL-aligned vocabulary.
Position:
- Keep the client dependency-free and modular to mirror the simplicity mandate in the spec.
- Separate the data model from rendering so we can evolve the UI without rewriting business rules.
Recommendations:
- Introduce a CalendarModel with explicit validation for time ranges and ownership to match backend invariants.
- Use pure template functions that emit semantic HTML for agenda, calendars, and insight cards.
- Ship seed data that reflects our core rituals to make the initial load meaningful and testable.
